  "body": "**Blocked by:** #108\n\n## Context\n\nActive modules must extend the queue and heartbeat scheduler without editing core enums.\n\n## Task\n\nAssemble runtime task names from immutable core names plus active module descriptors and register their payload schemas/handlers with the queue. Reject core overrides and duplicates. Extend scheduler validation with the union of core and active `heartbeatRuleKinds`; dispatch module-defined next-fire calculation through `nextFireAtExport`. Rebuild these consumptions consistently when activation state changes, without accepting a heartbeat/task whose module is inactive.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Task merge/registration and heartbeat rule validation/next-fire dispatch.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Queue engine implementation and service runner ownership.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Active module tasks enqueue and validate typed payloads.\n- Conflicting task names fail deterministically.\n- Module rule kinds schedule through their exported calculator.\n- Deactivated rule/task definitions cannot be newly dispatched.\n",
